    }
  ],
  "deloadRecommended": false,
  "deloadReason": null,
  "actionItems": [
    "Add at least 3 to 4 dedicated leg sets next week, targeting compound movements like squats or leg press, with the goal of getting legs to at least 10 to 15% of your weekly volume.",
    "Maintain the current loading progression on chest and back since both jumped 4 index points this period — continue adding small increments of weight or reps to sustain this momentum.",
    "Give biceps a small stimulus boost by either adding a fourth set or slightly increasing the load, as the index has stalled at 101 for two consecutive periods.",
    "Review your weekly session structure to ensure legs are scheduled early in the week when energy is highest, rather than being left as an afterthought or skipped entirely."
  ],
  "contextSummary": "Strong upper-body gains this period with chest and back each up 4 index points, but legs remain severely undertrained at 1 set and a flat baseline index of 100 — addressing leg volume is the top priority next period."
}
